<WovenDocs::Page
  @id="alert"
  @title="Alert"
  @subtitle="Inline message in five role colors, with optional description, actions and dismiss."
  @components="Woven::Alert"
>
  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Overview" @id="overview">
    <p class="woven-doc__intro">
      An alert reports a condition in place. It renders the CSS kit
      <code class="wu-code">wu-alert</code>, which draws its own marker shape,
      so there is no icon argument. Meaning is carried by the title text; the
      marker repeats it. Dismissal is a callback: the alert does not hide
      itself. For transient feedback after an action use a toast instead.
    </p>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Features" @id="features">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Five role colors plus a neutral default; success, warning and danger also change the marker shape.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Title and description, or custom block content.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Actions row and a labeled dismiss button.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Variants" @id="variants">
    {{#each this.variantExamples as |example|}}
      <WovenDocs::Example @title={{example.title}} @note={{example.note}} @layout="block" @code={{example.code}}>
        <Woven::Alert @variant={{example.variant}} @title="{{example.title}} alert" />
      </WovenDocs::Example>
    {{/each}}
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Content" @id="content">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Title and description"
      @note="The description adds a paragraph under the title. For anything the user needs a sentence to understand."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.description}}
    >
      <Woven::Alert
        @variant="success"
        @title="Rent collected"
        @description="AED 42,000 was collected across 6 units this week."
      />
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Block content"
      @note="A block replaces title and description for markup such as links and emphasis. Use the kit wu-alert-title part for the first line."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.block}}
    >
      <Woven::Alert @variant="warning">
        <strong class="wu-alert-title">Document expiring</strong>
        <p>The trade license for Marina Heights expires in <strong>12 days</strong>.</p>
      </Woven::Alert>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Actions"
      @note="The actions block renders the kit wu-alert-actions row, so the next step sits inside the alert and the user does not have to hunt for it."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.actions}}
    >
      <Woven::Alert
        @variant="warning"
        @title="Cheque bounced"
        @description="Post-dated cheque #4821 was returned by the bank."
      >
        <:actions>
          <Woven::Button @size="sm" @text="Contact tenant" />
          <Woven::Button @variant="ghost" @size="sm" @text="Dismiss" />
        </:actions>
      </Woven::Alert>
    </WovenDocs::Example>

    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Status role"
      @note="The alert renders role alert, which interrupts a screen reader. Pass role status for messages that are not urgent."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.status}}
    >
      <Woven::Alert @variant="info" @title="Sync scheduled" @description="Listings refresh every night at 02:00." role="status" />
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Dismissal" @id="dismissal">
    <WovenDocs::Example
      @title="Closable"
      @note="A labeled kit wu-alert-close button reports through onClose; render the alert conditionally so it is removed rather than hidden."
      @layout="block"
      @code={{this.code.closable}}
    >
      {{#if this.alertDismissed}}
        <div class="woven-row">
          <span class="wu-text sm muted">Danger alert dismissed.</span>
          <Woven::Button
            @variant="link"
            @size="sm"
            @text="Reset"
            @onClick={{this.resetAlert}}
            data-test-woven-alert-reset
          />
        </div>
      {{else}}
        <Woven::Alert
          @variant="danger"
          @title="Maintenance overdue"
          @description="Unit 118, JVC Residence has an unresolved AC repair ticket open for 9 days."
          @closable={{true}}
          @onClose={{this.dismissAlert}}
        />
      {{/if}}
    </WovenDocs::Example>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Arguments" @id="arguments">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="args" @rows={{this.argRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Callbacks" @id="callbacks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="callbacks" @rows={{this.callbackRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Blocks" @id="blocks">
    <WovenDocs::Table @kind="blocks" @rows={{this.blockRows}} />
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="Accessibility" @id="accessibility">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>Renders role="alert", so content is announced when it appears; pass role="status" for messages that are not urgent. Render alerts conditionally rather than toggling visibility.</span></li>
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The marker is drawn in CSS and has no text; the title carries the meaning. The dismiss button is labeled "Dismiss alert".</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>

  <WovenDocs::Section @title="RTL" @id="rtl">
    <ul class="wu-list sm" role="list">
      <li class="wu-list-item"><span>The kit lays out marker, content and dismiss button with logical properties, so the marker leads and the dismiss button sits in the end corner in both directions.</span></li>
    </ul>
  </WovenDocs::Section>
</WovenDocs::Page>
